# Shpati — Unified Lab Report Digitizer

Shpati combines the best engineering patterns from **Lerdi** (deterministic file storage, RapidOCR variant matrix, Vite API proxy) and **TrustLab** (10-stage pipeline, 3-tier clinical validation, human-in-the-loop review).

## Architecture

```
Shpati/
├── backend/          FastAPI + 10-stage async pipeline
├── frontend/         React 19 + Vite 6 + Tailwind 4
└── storage/          Local-first report folders by ID
```

| Layer | Source inspiration |
|-------|-------------------|
| `ReportStore` | Lerdi — one folder per report ID |
| Pipeline `s1`–`s10` | TrustLab — single-responsibility stages |
| OCR matrix | Lerdi — RapidOCR across OpenCV variants |
| Validation | TrustLab — `accepted` / `needs_review` / `rejected` |
| Review API | TrustLab — `/api/review/apply` provenance |
| Dev proxy | Lerdi — `/api` and `/media` via Vite |

## Quick start

### Backend (port 8000)

```bash
cd Shpati
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
shpati-api
```

### Frontend (port 3000)

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open **http://127.0.0.1:3000**

## API highlights

- `GET /api/health` — service status
- `GET /api/reports` — dashboard telemetry
- `POST /api/reports/upload` — ingest + run full pipeline
- `GET /api/reports/{id}` — structured report + lineage JSON
- `POST /api/review/session` — open human review session
- `POST /api/review/apply` — approve / edit / reject rows
- `POST /api/review/finalize` — rebuild FHIR from accepted rows

## Storage layout

Each upload is stored under `storage/uploaded_reports/` and processed into `storage/outputs/{report_id}/` with artifacts:

`ocr.json`, `layout.json`, `structured.json`, `fhir.json`, `evaluation.json`

## Tests

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
pytest backend/tests -q
```
